5. System Description  

5.1 Features and Functionality Included 

-The system includes the following key features: 

-Chat/Messaging System between Instructors and Students 

-Check-In/Out Feature 

-Attendance Tracking 

-Geolocation 

-Class Roster and Enrollment 

-Login/Logout 

-Navigation 

-User Roles for Students/Instructors/Admins 

-User-Friendly UI 

5.2 Feature Descriptions 

Chat/Messaging System 

    This feature enables Instructors and Students to communicate through a chat/messaging system. The system stores messages in the chat and allows group chat creation. 

Check-In/Out Feature 

    This feature enables users (Students) to check in to a single class. Check-ins for multiple classes at once are unavailable. Users must check-out before checking-in again. The system tracks check-in/out time, tracks longitude and latitude on check-in/out, and tracks and displays student ID. 

Attendance Tracking 

    Student attendance is tracked within a database, storing records of attendance events with timestamps, student ID, class ID, and geolocation data. 

 

Geolocation 

    Utilizes Abstract's IP Geolocation API that determines the location and other details of IP addresses. 

Class Roster and Enrollment 

    Instructors can view the class roster and chat or view details on students enrolled in their courses. 

    Login/Logout 

    Users can login and logout with assigned user roles, authentication, and IDs. 

Navigation 

    User access to messaging, attendance, and class features through the navigation menu. 

User Roles 
The system implements three distinct user roles with specific permissions: 

    Students: Can check in/out of their enrolled classes and communicate with Instructors and other students through the messaging system. 

    Instructors: Can create and delete classes, add or remove students from their classes, and communicate with students and other instructors through the messaging system.  

    Administrators: Can create or remove users such as instructors or students. 